<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21224] Linux 7.x kernel fixes</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21224</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Two fixes for newer Linux 7.x kernels:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;osd-ldiskfs fails to build at modpost on kernels without CONFIG_CRC_T10DIF (for example mainline 7.0 from defconfig, which has no BLK_DEV_INTEGRITY): obdclass defines obd_dif_crc_fn() and obd_dif_ip_fn() only with CRC_T10DIF, but osd_integrity.c uses them unconditionally. osc already handles this case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lst new_session oopses with a NULL dereference in lst_sessions_cmd() on Linux 7.1 and later. Since upstream commit b93ec16310b4 ("genetlink: use maxattr of 0 for the reject policy"), genetlink fills info-&amp;gt;attrs only for operations with a policy, and the lnet_selftest family has none.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Found while building and testing on mainline 7.0 and 7.3.4.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
